<title>UK: London silver fixes at lowest in over two years.</title>
<headline>London silver fixes at lowest in over two years.</headline>
<text>
<p>SILVER - Fixed at 464.25 cents vs 472.40 cents previously, lowest fixing since March 27, 1995. Technically bearish, weakened on fund selling post-option expiry.</p>
<p>GOLD - Fairly steady, nervous at $339.15/$339.45, down about 65 cents. Could try lower. Short positions building. Bearish tone.</p>
<p>PLATINUM - Steady at $372.50/$373.50, down $0.50.</p>
<p>PALLADIUM - Quiet at $0.50 firmer $157.25/$158.25.</p>
</text>
